  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A granny square dishcloth is a single 5-round granny motif about 20 cm across. Worked in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook, 5 rounds reach the right size for a dishcloth."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Starting with a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring-dc"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " gives a tightly closed centre. The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "granny-cl"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "granny clusters"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " make a firm, thick fabric. Total yarn needed is around 35 m."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK cotton yarn",
              "qty": "35 m (about 28 g)"
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Magic ring. Ch 3, 2 tr into ring (first cluster), ch 2. *3 tr into ring (cluster), ch 2*. Repeat 3 times. Sl st to top of ch 3. Pull ring closed. (4 clusters, 4 ch-2 corners.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st to corner space. Ch 3, 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr into same space (corner). *Ch 1, corner into next space*. Repeat. Ch 1. Sl st. (4 corners.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Rounds 3 to 5"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st to corner. Ch 3, 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr into corner. *Ch 1, 3 tr into each ch-1 side space with ch 1 between, ch 1, corner into corner space*. Repeat. Sl st. Each round adds one cluster per side."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fasten off after round 5. Secure all tails with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "weaving-in-ends"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "weaving in ends"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". No edging needed unless the edges look uneven."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash 60 degrees normal. Tumble dry or hang flat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work 5 rounds to a larger hook size for a bigger cloth. Or join two granny squares side by side for a longer rectangle cloth."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}